Engine-side note recorded during the A/B: stop_info_set (macos_api_mod.F90)
rejects iElt >= nElt-2, so on the 4-element rodgers3 decks the stop cannot
be bound to M2 even though the stop plane coincides with it (.seq th5 = 0).
The inserted Reference stop element is therefore REQUIRED by the veneer
path, which matches the template rule (emit a Reference at the stop plane).
The zero-distance Reference->M2 insert traces cleanly (negative-L
intersection allowed after a Reference element; ConSrf ifLNsrf).
